"Choose `ManagedEntity` or `RecordEntity` based on your use case.\n"
"The Managed Repository is more expressive, but reasoning about it is more complex and might require knowing some details about how Hibernate handles objects.\n"
"If you are an experienced Hibernate developer, you expect that changing an object's field does not immediately hit the database.\n"
"Some users prefer a more explicit way to control the database.\n"
"Both approaches are supported; choose based on your application's requirements."
msgstr "请根据您的具体用例选择 `ManagedEntity` 或 `RecordEntity` 。Managed Repository 的表达能力更强，但对其进行推理更为复杂，可能需要了解 Hibernate 处理对象的一些细节。 如果您是一位经验丰富的 Hibernate 开发人员，您会期望修改对象的字段不会立即影响数据库。有些用户则更倾向于采用更显式的方式来控制数据库。这两种方法均受支持；请根据应用程序的要求进行选择。"

msgid "Reactive"
msgstr "响应式"

#. mt: deepl
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you are already using reactive APIs in your application (Quarkus Messaging, reactive REST clients, Vert.x), you want your database access to compose naturally with them without blocking the event loop.\n"
"Choose blocking or reactive access to match your use case.\n"
"The same entity model works unchanged with a reactive driver."
msgstr "如果您已经在应用程序中使用了响应式 API（例如 Quarkus Messaging、响应式 REST 客户端、Vert.x），那么您希望数据库访问能够与它们自然地协同工作，同时不阻塞事件循环。请根据您的用例选择阻塞式或响应式访问方式。相同的实体模型在响应式驱动程序中无需任何修改即可正常工作。"

